  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Arithmetic Expressions"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.5,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Writing it as sum of terms gives:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.11,
            0.59,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.406,
                0.11,
                0.59,
                0.15
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.159,
            0.551,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This expression means 24 more than "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times 4 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . But, we want an expression which means twice or double of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 3 \\pm 2 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.215,
            0.551,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can make use of brackets to write such an expression:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.285,
            0.251,
            0.413,
            0.268
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "2 \\times ( 4 3 \\pm 2 4 ) ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.27,
            0.552,
            0.343
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, we can say that together they have to pay "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 \\times ( 4 3 \\pm 2 4 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This is also the same as paying for two vegetable cutlets and two rasgullas:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.343,
            0.425,
            0.36
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "2 \\times 4 3 + 2 \\times 2 4 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.361,
            0.262,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.385,
            0.495,
            0.403
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "2 \\times (43 + 24) = 2 \\times 43 + 2 \\times 24."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.577,
            0.15,
            0.901,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.577,
                0.15,
                0.901,
                0.405
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_10.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.413,
            0.848,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? If another friend, Sangmu, joins them and orders the same items, what will be the expression for the total amount to be paid?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.462,
            0.848,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 16:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In the Republic Day parade, there are boy scouts and girl guides marching together. The scouts march in 4 rows with 5 scouts in each row. The guides march in 3 rows with 5 guides in each row (see the figure below). How many scouts and guides are marching in this parade?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.56,
            0.848,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The number of boy scouts marching is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . The number of girl guides marching is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\times 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.599,
            0.415,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The total number of scouts and guides will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 5 + 3 \\times 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.653,
            0.416,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can also be found by first finding the total number of rows, i.e., 4 + 3, and then multiplying their sum by the number of children in each row. Thus, the number of boys and girls can be found by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "(4 + 3) \\times 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.437,
            0.596,
            0.877,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.437,
                0.596,
                0.877,
                0.819
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.819,
            0.415,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 5 + 3 \\times 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.837,
            0.272,
            0.854
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "= ( 4 + 3 ) \\times 5 ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.856,
            0.545,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Computing these expressions, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.875,
            0.813,
            0.918
          ],
          "content": [
            {
